\f0\fs24 \cf0 I need you to build a "SST Demo Engine" sidecar module for my Node.js SaaS app. This module must be isolated from production logic and must be safe by design.\
\
Feature flag (Kill Switch)\
- Everything in this module must be gated by ENV ENABLE_DEMO_MODE=true.\
- If false, POST /api/demo/check-in must return 404 (or 403), and housekeeping must not run.\
\
The Strategy: "Hotel Room Model"\
- We have 10 reusable demo rooms mapped to Company IDs 1001..1010, cloned from the Golden Master company ID 999.\
- A prospect can \'93check in\'94 and receive access to exactly one room.\
- A room expires at the next 2:00 AM in timezone America/Bogota, and then must be wiped and re-cloned from 999.\
\
1) Database schema\
Create table demo_room_bookings with:\
- room_id INT PRIMARY KEY (1..10)\
- company_id INT UNIQUE NOT NULL (1001..1010)\
- demo_user_email TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL (demo1@sst.com .. demo10@sst.com)\
- status TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('AVAILABLE','OCCUPIED','RESETTING','ERROR'))\
- assigned_prospect_id TEXT NULL (random uuid or session id)\
- assigned_prospect_email TEXT NULL\
- expires_at TIMESTAMPTZ NULL\
- updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\
\
Include CHECK constraints so company_id must be between 1001 and 1010.\
\
2) Sidecar structure\
- All code must live in src/modules/demo_hotel/\
- Provide a function assertSafeDemoCompanyId(companyId) that throws unless 1001..1010.\
- IMPORTANT: resetCompanyData must ALSO call assertSafeDemoCompanyId internally (not just the controller).\
\
3) API endpoint: POST /api/demo/check-in\
- If ENABLE_DEMO_MODE is false. refuse.\
- Input: optional prospect email\
- Output: credentials OR a magic login token (prefer token if feasible)\
\
Critical: prevent race conditions.\
Implement check-in as a DB transaction that atomically assigns ONE available room:\
- Use SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED (Postgres) or an atomic UPDATE ... RETURNING approach so two users cannot get the same room.\
Flow:\
a) Find an AVAILABLE room and lock it.\
b) Mark status=RESETTING and set assigned_prospect_id, expires_at = next 2:00 AM America/Bogota.\
c) Call resetCompanyData(sourceCompanyId=999, targetCompanyId=selectedCompanyId) inside the same overall logical flow.\
d) If reset succeeds. set status=OCCUPIED.\
e) If reset fails. set status=ERROR and return an error.\
\
If no room is available:\
- Either implement a simple queue table demo_waitlist (optional), or return 503 with Retry-After: 300 and message \'93All demo rooms are currently in use.\'94\
\
4) Housekeeping job\
- Use node-cron.\
- Run every hour.\
- If ENABLE_DEMO_MODE is false, do nothing.\
- Find rooms where status='OCCUPIED' and expires_at < now().\
- For each room, set status=RESETTING, run resetCompanyData(999, company_id), then set status=AVAILABLE and clear assigned_prospect fields and expires_at.\
- If reset fails, set status=ERROR and log with details.\
\
5) resetCompanyData requirements\
- Must be fully transactional. If any step fails, rollback completely.\
- Must be idempotent (safe to run multiple times).\
- Must never delete or modify any company outside 1001..1010.\
- Clearly list which tables are wiped/cloned (ask the codebase, inspect schema, and implement based on existing relations).\
\
Deliverables\
- SQL migration for demo_room_bookings (and demo_waitlist if you implement queue)\
- checkIn controller + route wiring\
- node-cron job setup\
- resetCompanyData transactional implementation (or integration with existing clone logic)\
- Basic structured logging and error handling for auditing\
}